# The launch canary: no commands at all, just whatever the visual boots into.
#
# No golden — the default look animates, so it is not pixel-stable by construction.
# What this scene proves is the thing that breaks most often and costs the most round
# trips: the visual came up, built its pipelines, drew a real frame, and is still
# advancing its clock. A pipeline/bind-group mismatch (#519) fails here, at frame one,
# with a log — not three sessions later.
#!desc    Boots to the default look, draws a live frame, and keeps animating.
#!checks  nonblack,animates
#!settle  1200
